  "findings": "This legacy generic woodland-fern profile uses male fern as its documented architectural analogue, not a separate botanical species. Inspected upright crown and outward frond habit, then pinna structure in the underside detail; sori serve as structural reference only. Compared current small/medium/large pilots 1/4/7 and complete 36 sheet. Explicit curved rachises, tapering pinnae and aligned secondary pinnules give separate fronds and varied rosette openness. Heights approximately 0.33-0.68 m; 25 mm merges the fine pinnules in smaller fronds, an acknowledged stylization. Accepted the spring green archetype with no separate reproductive structures.",
